From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:16:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] qt: fix mouse wheel axis and rotation

Scrolling down was reported as a horizontal wheel event with zero rotation,
because the axis test only accepted positive vertical deltas. The rotation
was also divided by 8 while m_wheelDelta stays 120; Qt's angleDelta() already
uses 120 per notch, so pass it through unscaled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PMkXiZQmqtvCJRtsVHJjyT
---
 src/qt/window.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/qt/window.cpp b/src/qt/window.cpp
index 5078257..c59a043 100644
--- a/src/qt/window.cpp
+++ b/src/qt/window.cpp
@@ -1631,10 +1631,14 @@ bool wxWindowQt::QtHandleWheelEvent ( QWidget *WXUNUSED( handler ), QWheelEvent
     wxMouseEvent e( wxEVT_MOUSEWHEEL );
 #if (QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 15, 0))
     QPoint qPt = event->position().toPoint();
-    wxMouseWheelAxis wheelAxis = event->angleDelta().y() > 0
+    // angleDelta() is in eighths of a degree, 120 per wheel notch, which is the same
+    // convention as wxMouseEvent::m_wheelDelta, so it is used unscaled. Any non-zero
+    // vertical component (in either direction) makes this a vertical wheel event.
+    const QPoint angleDelta = event->angleDelta();
+    wxMouseWheelAxis wheelAxis = angleDelta.y() != 0
                                ? wxMOUSE_WHEEL_VERTICAL : wxMOUSE_WHEEL_HORIZONTAL;
     int wheelRotation = wheelAxis == wxMOUSE_WHEEL_VERTICAL
-                      ? (event->angleDelta().y() / 8) : (event->angleDelta().x() / 8);
+                      ? angleDelta.y() : angleDelta.x();
 #else
     QPoint qPt = event->pos();
     wxMouseWheelAxis wheelAxis = event->orientation() == Qt::Vertical
